# Isolated copies of the repo, one per provider, created by src/domain/pi-agent/worktree.js.
# Working space: git worktree already refuses to track them, but the parent dir is ours.
.bigkiji/

# ── 公開リポジトリに載せないもの（2026-08-05）─────────────────────
# 運用プレイブック。アプリのコードではなく、オーナー環境の手順書。
# 中には社内の実パスや姉妹事業の名前が入っている。skill-registry.js は
# ~/.claude/skills も読むので、ここに無くてもアプリは動く。
# `/skills/*` rather than `/skills/`: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a negation under it never gets a chance to match.
/skills/*
# …except the one the app itself depends on. bku-check is not a playbook about the
# owner's environment; it is the rule the agent has to carry to behave correctly, and
# check-folder-selftest fails without it. It names no sister business and no path that
# src/core/path-config.js does not already state in the open.
!/skills/bku-check/
# Same reasoning for lesson-video. It is not a playbook about the owner's machine; it is
# what stops the agent from building a unit the course already teaches (measured
# 2026-08-07: a whole unit was designed as a 100% duplicate of u03 and u07 before anyone
# opened content/materials/thailand.ts) and from re-generating characters that already
# exist. Losing it costs a duplicate unit, which is the expensive kind of mistake here.
!/skills/lesson-video/
# 第三者の動画9本のフレーム単位解析。画面内のコードと字幕を逐語転記しており、
# 他人の著作物の複製にあたる。設計判断の根拠としてローカルには残す。
/docs/reference-analysis.md
# 社内の役割サンドボックス構成と内部監査の引用。
/AI_ORGANIZATION_HANDBOOK.md

# Run ledger detail. On disk on purpose (a pi agent reads it there),
# but one line per run is not worth a diff. The .md beside it IS tracked.
docs/v3/run-ledger.jsonl
